\title{Modal simplicial type theory formalised in Agda}
\author{samueltoth}
\taxon{Reference}
\date{2026-04-15}
\meta{venue}{[[unott]]}
\meta{external}{https://samtoth.github.io/ModalSTTInAgda.pdf}

\p{
We present a formalised library of simplicial homotopy type theory in the proof assistant
Agda. This builds on the foundations developed in the original work on simplicial
type theory by Riehl and Shulman [RS17]; however, unlike existing formalisations
[KRW23], we follow the approach of Gratzer, Weinberger, and Buchholtz [GWB26a;
GWB25] working pervasively only up to equivalence, as well as incorporating modal
type theory in order to construct a non-trivial example of a synthetic category. To make
this possible, a pair of prototype extensions to the Agda programming language have
been developed. The latter extension, implementing that sharp modality of Shulman’s
Cohesive Type Theory [Shu18], has now been merged into the main branch of Agda.
We discuss the key results in the library, in particular the formalisation of a directed
univalent universe of Spaces [GWB26a].
}

